sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: abandon only an intact failed development Instance removal.
  %% Tightened: admission evidence, exact fence settlement, shared Route create children, compensation before hold release.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:restore
  %% kind: instance.restore
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Target Nodes<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: instance:restore INSTANCE
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the numeric development Instance ID
  Note over GW: Lock, inspect survivors
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - lock the Instance, removal, databases and Route publication
  %%> - the latest live removal failed and all its native runs conclusively stopped
  %%> - no queued, running or waiting lifecycle, Process or Schedule work
  %%> - one bounded source read proves checkout, workspace and Git identity
  %%> - an admin catalog read proves every planned database, user and ownership
  alt already restored
    %% path: already-restored
    GW-->>CLI: instance.already_restored
    %%> Result:
    %%> - verify the successful restoration receipt and current active records; return the stable skip
  else admission refuses
    %% path: refused
    GW--xCLI: Named refusal
    %%> Result:
    %%> - identify the missing resource, irreversible step or drift; no restore Operation or publication
  else intact failed removal
    %% path: main
    GW->>SW: Start restore run<br/>operation-instance-restore
    %%> Captures:
    %%> - this removal's own verified journal rows, Route and targets
    %%> - keep the Instance removing and the removal failed/live
    %%> - keep publication holds until terminal compensation settles
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted
    %%> Result:
    %%> - follow the instance.restore Operation
    SW->>N: Settle database fences<br/>Ansible · settle
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - delete only captured matching name, OID and allow-connections rows; already absent succeeds
    %%> - refuse identity or admission drift; no ALTER and no schema-wide delete
    SW->>N: Republish the Route<br/>operation-route-create
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reuse the CSR, sign, site, TLS and DNS children with the same Route, targets and domain
    %%> - the existing site phase writes only the awake marker
    %%> - TLS publication and its check complete before active records
    alt publication and check pass
      %% path: restored
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded
      %%> Result:
      %%> - project only the bound terminal run
      Note over GW: Commit restored records
      %%> Result:
      %%> - in one transaction: members abandoned_at, removal abandoned with step/error fields cleared, Instance active and Route active/published
      %%> - preserve removal inventory, deletion receipts and old failed Operations
      GW-->>CLI: Instance restored
      %%> Result:
      %%> - a later destroy captures a fresh identity and inventory
    else execution fails
      %% path: failed
      SW->>N: Compensate publication<br/>Ansible · marker, withdrawal
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - remove a newly written awake marker and withdraw a partial site and DNS before releasing publication holds
      %%> - preserve checkout, databases and completed fence settlement
      SW--xGW: Run failed
      %%> Result:
      %%> - Instance removing, removal failed/live and restore Operation failed
      %%> - expose compensation failure; a fresh restore attempt is repeatable
    end
  end
